# pg_durable

pg_durable adds durable, fault-tolerant SQL workflows to PostgreSQL. Workflow
state is stored in PostgreSQL, and a background worker resumes execution after
crashes, restarts, and transient failures without an external orchestrator.

```sql
SELECT df.start(
    'SELECT id FROM documents WHERE processed = false LIMIT 100' |=> 'batch'
    ~> 'UPDATE documents SET processed = true WHERE id IN (SELECT id FROM $batch.*)'
);
```

Start with the
[User Guide](https://pgxn.org/dist/pg_durable/@CARGO_VERSION@/USER_GUIDE.html)
and [API Reference](https://pgxn.org/dist/pg_durable/@CARGO_VERSION@/docs/api-reference.html).
See the
[examples overview](https://pgxn.org/dist/pg_durable/@CARGO_VERSION@/examples/README.html),
[HTTP security guide](https://pgxn.org/dist/pg_durable/@CARGO_VERSION@/docs/http-security.html),
and [changelog](https://pgxn.org/dist/pg_durable/@CARGO_VERSION@/CHANGELOG.html)
for focused guidance. The project website is
[microsoft.github.io/pg_durable](https://microsoft.github.io/pg_durable/).

## Install from PGXN

PGXN distributes source, not binaries. Installation requires PostgreSQL 17 or
18 development files, Rust, pgxnclient, and cargo-pgrx 0.16.1:

```bash
cargo install --locked cargo-pgrx --version 0.16.1
pgxn install --sudo -- pg_durable
```

The `--` separator prevents `pg_durable` from being consumed as the optional
program argument to `--sudo`. The build runs as your user; only installation
into PostgreSQL's system directories is elevated.

Add `pg_durable` to `shared_preload_libraries`, restart PostgreSQL, and enable
the extension:

```sql
CREATE EXTENSION pg_durable;
SELECT df.grant_usage('app_role');
```

When upgrading, install the new files, restart PostgreSQL, then update the
extension schema in the configured pg_durable database:

```sql
ALTER EXTENSION pg_durable UPDATE TO '@CARGO_VERSION@';
```

Prebuilt Debian packages and evaluation Docker images are available from
[GitHub releases](https://github.com/microsoft/pg_durable/releases).
